Requirements: 15   with obligations: 14   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] A criterion's test-evidence rating comes from the ways it could fail. The
    review already records, for each criterion, the ways a change could fail it, and for
    each of those and each candidate test, whether that test would fail if the delivered
    code failed that way. Those recorded judgements now decide the rating a criterion
    gets, the tests the review recommends and the conclusion it reaches; the older
    judgement of which tests bear on which criterion, and of whether each of those tests
    discriminates, is removed.
    -> criterion-rating-derived-from-failure-modes  [invariant/explicit]
       A criterion's test-evidence rating is determined from the ways it could fail.
    -> record-criterion-failure-modes  [invariant/explicit]
       The review already records, for each criterion, the ways a change could fail it.
    -> candidate-tests-fail-on-each-failure-way  [functional/explicit]
       For each recorded way the delivered code could fail a criterion, and for each
       candidate test, determine whether that test would fail if the code failed that
       way.
    -> tests-the-review-recommends  [test_demand/explicit]
       The review recommends tests.
    -> conclusion-it-reaches  [functional/explicit]
       The review's conclusion is determined by the recorded judgements about how the
       criterion could fail and how candidate tests would fail under those failures.
    -> remove-older-judgement-of-test-bearings  [regression/explicit]
       Remove the older judgement of which tests bear on which criterion.
    -> remove-older-judgement-of-test-discrimination  [regression/explicit]
       Remove the older judgement of whether each of those tests discriminates.
    -> remove-discrimination-judgement  [regression/explicit]
       The change removes the judgement of whether each candidate test discriminates.

[constraint-01] A recorded way of failing is covered when some candidate test would fail
    if the delivered code failed that way. A criterion all of whose recorded ways of
    failing are covered is strongly supported; one where some are covered is partially
    supported; one where none are, while candidate tests exist, is nominally supported.
    Where no candidate test exists, or the judgement could not be reached, the outcomes
    the review already has for those cases stand.
    -> coverage-from-failing-way  [functional/explicit]
       A recorded way of failing is covered when some candidate test would fail if the
       delivered code failed that way.
    -> rating-by-coverage-completeness  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion all of whose recorded ways of failing are covered is strongly
       supported; one where some are covered is partially supported; one where none are,
       while candidate tests exist, is nominally supported.
    -> preserve-existing-outcomes-when-unevaluable  [invariant/explicit]
       Where no candidate test exists, or the judgement could not be reached, the
       outcomes the review already has for those cases stand.

[constraint-02] Every rating the report shows names how many of that criterion's
    recorded ways of failing are covered, and how many were recorded.
    -> rating-shows-covered-and-total-failures  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       Every report rating names how many of the criterion's recorded ways of failing
       are covered, and how many were recorded.

[constraint-03] A criterion for which the review recorded no plausible way of failing,
    and said why, gets an outcome of its own, neither strongly supported nor
    unsupported, and the report says test evidence cannot be obtained for it.
    -> no-plausible-failure-outcome  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion with no recorded plausible way of failing, and with an explanation
       for that, receives its own outcome that is neither strongly supported nor
       unsupported, and the report states that test evidence cannot be obtained for it.

[constraint-04] Every test the review recommends names one recorded way of failing that
    no candidate test would fail on, and that record carries a link to the criterion
    text it comes from.
    -> recommended-test-names-failing-way  [test_demand/explicit]
       Every recommended test names one recorded way of failing that no candidate test
       would fail on, and the recommendation includes a link to the criterion text it
       comes from.

[constraint-05] A recommendation asking for evidence the review already holds cannot be
    produced.
    -> no-redundant-recommendation  [functional/explicit]
       A recommendation that asks for evidence the review already holds is not produced.

[constraint-06] The ratings keep the names they have today.
    -> keep-rating-names  [compatibility/explicit]
       The ratings keep the names they have today.

[constraint-07] Where the review's measured accuracy is reported, that report says the
    figures do not span this change.
    -> accuracy-report-does-not-span-change  [docs_config/explicit]
       Where the review's measured accuracy is reported, the report states that the
       figures do not span this change.

[constraint-08] Two recorded runs over the same input produce byte-identical review
    state and byte-identical report output.
    -> deterministic-runs-byte-identical  [invariant/explicit]
       Two recorded runs over the same input produce byte-identical review state and
       byte-identical report output.

[exclusion-01] Recording the ways a criterion could fail, and judging one of them
    against a candidate test.
    -> no-recording-or-judging-failures  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not include recording the ways a criterion could fail, or judging
       one of those ways against a candidate test.

[exclusion-02] Which criteria the review derives from the mandate, and how it derives
    them.
    -> do-not-change-criterion-derivation  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not alter which criteria the review derives from the mandate or
       how it derives them.

[exclusion-03] Renaming a rating, or rewording what a rating means.
    -> keep-rating-names-and-meanings-unchanged  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not alter any rating names or reword what any rating means.

[exclusion-04] Running the delivered code or any test.
    -> no-running-delivered-code-or-tests  [human_review/explicit]
       The change does not involve running the delivered code or any test.

